WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.030
Night.

2
00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.230
A man sits all alone.

3
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:05.880
Everyone else has turned
their back on him.

4
00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:09.500
Out of luck, and out of
favour, he curses his fate,

5
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.600
and envies other men.

6
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:17.030
In the last line, the same man says:
"That then I scorn to change my state with

7
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.300
kings."

8
00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.410
Same man.

9
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:20.700
Same sonnet.

10
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.800
So what changes his mind?

11
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.020
In this mission, you'll
trace the sonnet's two moods:

12
00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.050
low, then rising.

13
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.690
You'll watch a lark climb
from the dark earth,

14
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.500
up to "heaven's gate".

15
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.760
And you'll see why this
sonnet, printed in 1609,

16
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.170
is all one long sentence.

17
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: work out
what changes his mind.
